3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,340
They give it to their friends first, then use the rest to buy weapons you didn't ask for.

4
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:20,770
By the time it reaches you, it buys less. This has been happening for a century.

5
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:25,540
Nobody covers it on the news because it is, by design, extremely boring.

6
00:00:26,180 --> 00:00:31,120
Dollar purchasing power retained since nineteen thirteen: four percent.

7
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:36,060
Unpopular wars funded without democratic consent: all of them.

8
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:44,200
This is a systems analysis. On Wishonia, we used rocks as currency for about four hundred years.

9
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:48,080
Then someone pointed out that rocks are heavy and also everywhere.

10
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:55,600
It took us another two hundred years of arguing, a bribery program, and three currency collapses before we switched to a

11
00:00:55,600 --> 00:01:03,140
shared ledger: a network of computers that all keep the same record of who has what, and check each other's work so nobody

12
00:01:03,260 --> 00:01:12,220
can lie. If one computer tries to say "actually I have a million extra coins," the other computers say "no you don't" and

13
00:01:12,220 --> 00:01:18,640
ignore it. That's the whole thing. It is not complicated. A child could understand it.

14
00:01:18,780 --> 00:01:24,010
(On Wishonia, a child *did* invent it. She was eleven. She won a science fair.

15
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:31,760
The previous monetary system had been designed by four hundred adults over two centuries and was worse in every way.).

16
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:39,820
Humans invented the same idea in two thousand and nine. It is called "blockchain," which is a word designed to make a simple

17
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:46,880
concept sound difficult, because if people understood how simple it was, they might ask why they're still using the old

18
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:52,620
system. Mostly, your species used it to buy drugs and expensive monkey JPGs.

19
00:01:53,540 --> 00:02:00,320
(You paid sixty-nine million dollars for a non-fungible token, or N.F.T., of a picture of an ape.

20
00:02:00,860 --> 00:02:06,970
The ape was not even real. I checked.). I will come back to this invention later, because it is important.

21
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:11,100
It makes the system I'm about to describe completely unnecessary.

22
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:17,840
But first, let me describe the system, because you are currently inside it and it is eating you.

23
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:26,060
Your species also used rocks as currency, except you picked the shiniest rock, dug it out of the ground at great expense,

24
00:02:26,780 --> 00:02:30,600
