31
00:03:04,300 --> 00:03:07,950
These twelve people are not elected. You did not pick them.

32
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:12,200
You do not know their names. (Go ahead. Try to name three. I'll wait.

33
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:21,640
You can't. Nobody can. This is a feature, not a bug.) They decide whether your money is worth more or less tomorrow, which

34
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:26,620
determines whether you can afford your rent, your groceries, your medicine, and your children's future.

35
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:35,100
Twelve people. One table. Eight meetings a year. This is your species' system for deciding who gets what.

36
00:03:35,740 --> 00:03:41,560
It has been running for over a century. It has funded the deaths of ninety-seven million people.

37
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:47,340
It is, by design, extremely boring, because boring things don't get investigated.

38
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:52,440
On Wishonia we have a word for making theft too tedious to investigate.

39
00:03:52,900 --> 00:04:00,200
It translates roughly to "beige crime.". I mentioned the network of computers that check each other so nobody can lie.

40
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:08,420
Your twelve-person table is the opposite of that. It is a network of humans who do not check each other, are not checked

41
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:17,300
